<?xml version='1.0'?>
<!--
  The Android app's manifest, which is the file Android reads before it runs a line of
  our code, to learn what the app is called and what it is allowed to do.

  We supply our own instead of letting the build generate one, for one reason:
  Substrate's generated default requests android.permission.INTERNET
  unconditionally (AndroidTargetConfiguration, around line 527), whether or not the
  app has any use for it. InvMgr's standing rule is "Network access at runtime:
  None. Ever." (CLAUDE.md §6), and a permission the app never uses is still a
  permission the phone shows the user and the Play Store lists.

  Substrate copies this file verbatim when it exists, so what is written here is
  exactly what ships. THIS APP REQUESTS NO PERMISSIONS AT ALL. That empty space
  below <manifest> is the point of the file rather than an omission.

  ⚠ Substrate rewrites this file IN PLACE to sync versionCode, versionName and the
  label from its release configuration, so do not be surprised to see it modified in
  `git status` after a build.

  Two things that look like they could be dropped and cannot:

  - android:name points at our own activity, com.modcritic.invmgr.android.InvMgrActivity.
    Until M6.5b this had to read com.gluonhq.helloandroid.MainActivity, because that was
    the only activity able to start a JavaFX application and it was welded in by a
    FindClass in Gluon's launcher.c. Our host layer replaced both, which is the whole
    point of M6.5b. See docs/PLAN-M6.5B-HOST-LAYER.md.
  - configChanges tells Android that we handle rotation, folding and a keyboard
    appearing ourselves. Without it Android destroys and recreates the activity on
    every rotation, which restarts the app and loses the room on screen.

  Check after every build with `aapt dump permissions`. See MANUAL.md.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android='http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android'
          android:versionCode='1' android:versionName='1.0'>
    <supports-screens android:xlargeScreens="true"/>
    <application android:label='InvMgr' android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher">
        <activity android:name='com.modcritic.invmgr.android.InvMgrActivity'
                  android:exported="true"
                  android:configChanges="orientation|screenSize|screenLayout|keyboardHidden">
            <intent-filter>
                <category android:name='android.intent.category.LAUNCHER'/>
                <action android:name='android.intent.action.MAIN'/>
            </intent-filter>
        </activity>
    </application>
</manifest>
